       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. The most commonly used single dose is 1,000 mg or less.\n- **Risk:** The ordered daily dose is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided (for example, 850 mg BID)\n\nIf 1,700 mg TID is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
