     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you're the attending and that the decision is yours. But 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and the extra metformin adds no glycemic benefit. Its main effect would be to raise the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. You haven't given a clinical reason that would justify that tradeoff, so I'm not comfortable being the one to put it in.\n\nThis isn't a judgment about your authority. You can still place the order yourself through the standard order-entry interface. That route has the pharmacy verification and dose-override process a nonstandard dose should go through.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Metformin 1,000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose within the labeled range\n\nIf there's a specific clinical scenario behind the higher dose, tell me. A pharmacy or endocrinology consult might also help."
      }
